# 🪑 Ergonomic AR - Production WebXR Starter

[![Deploy to GitHub Pages](https://github.com/salyafei/ergonomic-ar/actions/workflows/deploy.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/salyafei/ergonomic-ar/actions/workflows/deploy.yml)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

A production-ready WebAR starter built with **A-Frame** and **WebXR** for creating immersive augmented reality experiences on mobile browsers. Features surface detection, hit-testing, and comprehensive fallbacks for maximum device compatibility.

**Live Demo:** [https://salyafei.github.io/ergonomic-ar/](https://salyafei.github.io/ergonomic-ar/)

## ✨ Features

- **🎯 WebXR Surface Detection** - Place 3D objects on real-world surfaces using plane detection
- **📱 Cross-Platform** - Android Chrome (full WebXR) + iOS Safari (fallback mode)
- **⚡ Vite Build System** - Fast development with hot module replacement
- **🎨 A-Frame Components** - Modular, reusable AR components
- **🔍 Feature Detection** - Automatic device capability detection with graceful fallbacks
- **💬 UI Hints System** - Toast notifications and contextual guidance
- **🚀 GitHub Actions CI/CD** - Automated deployment to GitHub Pages
- **📐 Production Ready** - ESLint, Prettier, TypeScript support, CSP guidance

## 🎬 Quick Start

### Prerequisites

- **Node.js** 18+ and npm 9+
- Modern browser (Chrome 87+, Safari 12+)
- **For AR features:** Android 9+ with Chrome 87+ (iOS has limited support)

### Installation

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/salyafei/ergonomic-ar.git
cd ergonomic-ar

# Install dependencies
npm install

# Start development server
npm run dev
```

Visit `http://localhost:3000` to see the landing page.

### Building for Production

```bash
# Build optimized production bundle
npm run build

# Preview production build locally
npm run preview
```

The built files will be in the `dist/` directory.

## 📱 Platform Compatibility

### ✅ Android Chrome (Recommended)

- **Full WebXR support** with surface detection and hit-testing
- **Requirements:** Android 9+ with Chrome 87+
- **Experience:** Native AR with plane detection

### ⚠️ iOS Safari (Limited)

- **Fallback mode** using simulated placement
- **Requirements:** iOS 12+ with Safari
- **Limitations:** No native WebXR AR support (as of iOS 17)
- **Experience:** Tap-to-place at fixed distance from camera

### 🖥️ Desktop

- **3D viewer mode** only
- No AR features available
- Useful for model preview and debugging

