├── .eslintrc.json              # ESLint configuration
├── .prettierrc                 # Prettier configuration
└── README.md
```

## 🎨 Usage

### Adding Custom 3D Models

1. **Prepare your model:**
   - Export as `.glb` (GLTF Binary)
   - Recommended: Use DRACO compression
   - Keep file size < 5MB for mobile

2. **Add to assets:**
   ```bash
   cp your-model.glb public/assets/models/
   ```

3. **Update the scene:**
   ```html
   <!-- In src/scenes/surface-detection.html -->
   <a-assets>
     <a-asset-item id="your-model" src="/assets/models/your-model.glb"></a-asset-item>
   </a-assets>

   <!-- In placement template -->
   <a-entity data-template gltf-model="#your-model"></a-entity>
   ```

### Creating Custom AR Components

```javascript
// src/components/my-component.js
AFRAME.registerComponent('my-component', {
  schema: {
    color: { type: 'color', default: '#fff' }
  },

  init() {
    // Component initialization
  },

  tick(time, deltaTime) {
    // Called every frame
  }
});
```

Then import in your scene:
```html
<script type="module" src="../components/my-component.js"></script>
```

## 🔧 Configuration

### Vite Base Path

For GitHub Pages deployment, update `vite.config.js`:

```javascript
export default defineConfig({
  base: '/your-repo-name/',  // Match your repository name
  // ...
});
```

### Content Security Policy

For production, add CSP meta tag in `index.html`:

```html
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="
  default-src 'self';
  script-src 'self' 'nonce-RANDOM_NONCE' https://aframe.io;
  style-src 'self' 'nonce-RANDOM_NONCE';
  img-src 'self' data: blob:;
  connect-src 'self';
  font-src 'self' data:;
  media-src 'self' blob:;
  worker-src 'self' blob:;
">
```

## 🚀 Deployment

### GitHub Pages (Automated)

1. **Enable GitHub Pages:**
   - Go to repository Settings → Pages
   - Source: "GitHub Actions"

2. **Push to main branch:**
   ```bash
   git push origin main
   ```

3. **GitHub Actions will:**
   - Install dependencies
   - Run linter
   - Build production bundle
   - Deploy to `gh-pages`

Your site will be live at: `https://username.github.io/ergonomic-ar/`

### Manual Deployment

```bash
npm run build
# Upload the dist/ folder to your hosting provider
```

## 📝 Scripts

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `npm run dev` | Start development server on port 3000 |
| `npm run build` | Build production bundle |
| `npm run preview` | Preview production build locally |
| `npm run lint` | Lint code with ESLint |
| `npm run format` | Format code with Prettier |
| `npm run format:check` | Check code formatting |

## 🎯 Performance Optimization

### Model Optimization

```bash
# Install gltf-pipeline
npm install -g gltf-pipeline

# Compress with DRACO
gltf-pipeline -i model.glb -o model-compressed.glb -d
```

### Image Optimization

- Use WebP format for textures
- Maximum texture size: 2048x2048
- Power-of-two dimensions (512, 1024, 2048)

### Lazy Loading

Models are loaded only when needed:
```javascript
// In A-Frame assets
<a-assets timeout="30000">
  <a-asset-item id="model" src="/assets/models/model.glb"></a-asset-item>
</a-assets>
```

## 🐛 Troubleshooting

### Camera Permission Denied

**iOS:**
1. Tap "aA" in address bar
2. Website Settings → Camera → Allow
3. Reload page

**Android:**
1. Tap lock icon in address bar
2. Permissions → Camera → Allow
3. Reload page

### WebXR Not Supported (iOS)

This is expected. iOS Safari doesn't fully support WebXR AR. The app automatically falls back to simulated placement mode.

### Build Errors

```bash
# Clear node_modules and reinstall
rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json
npm install

# Clear Vite cache
rm -rf node_modules/.vite
npm run dev
```

